    "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Consider a sensing detection threshold ρ in (42), the maximum sensing range of an OFDM-ISAC system can be obtained by solving γ ( d ) = ρ , since the sensing SINR γ ( d ) is a monotonically decreasing function of d . Let ρ = 10 , the maximum sensing range is calculated to be 610m for the default CP length in Table I, which is much larger than the ISI free range 88.44m. Fig. 12 plots the change of the maximum sensing range with CP length. It is observed that if the CP is totally removed, i.e., T cp = 0 , the maximum sensing range can still reach about 590m for M = 14 . Besides, the maximum sensing range increases from 610m to 800m when the CP length increases from 0 . 59 µs to 5 . 3 µs , due to the reduced power degradation and ISI/ICI. For d > 800 m, the received"
